{
  "comment": [
    "Descriptors of the accessors in accessors/ that the registry does not publish",
    "(committed there, see README.MD). The registry's index cannot describe them, so",
    "\"Test your own file\" reads this next to it and says, for these, that the build is",
    "local. \"using\" comes from the accessor's manifest in the player tree; null means",
    "it was not found there and the tester then assumes the full solver only.",
    "Publishing an accessor removes its entry here.",
    "Where the manifest stopped at mm_solver_1.0.4, 1.0.5 is added here: its dynamic-linking",
    "surface is identical to 1.0.4's (checked on both binaries), which is the evidence the",
    "\"using\" rule asks for.",
    "1.0.6 is added the same way: its surface is identical to 1.0.5's (only the WebCodecs",
    "encoder, inside the main module, changed).",
    "Encoders (ffmpeg-x264, libx265, libmp3lame) are left out: they declare the format they",
    "produce, and the tester, which only assembles decoding pipelines, would otherwise pick",
    "them as decoders - ffmpeg-x264_1 claiming AVC broke the H.264 test that way."
  ],
